    "teaserText": "Archery",
    "startText": "The three fellows had vanished, naturally.[scoffs] \nCowards tend to be surprisingly good at this. [pause] [frustrated] Anthony had lost his peace, most of his wine and whatever little faith he had left in married life. [determined] By sunrise, Anthony had reached for his father's bow. It was time to have a talk with the fellows, [determined] preferably from a distance.",
    "winText": "[proud] The arrows struck near their feet and Anthony felt better. \n\n[repelled]But by the end of the week, Anthony's domestic difficulties had become public entertainment. His wife had left, the neighbours had developed a remarkable interest in avoiding him.\n\n[disappointed] The women have had their chance. [curious] Perhaps the army has lower standards.",
    "loseText": "The bow is a weapon, not a means of expressing one's feelings to the countryside. Take the high ground, judge your distance and aim carefully. The gods have given you two eyes for a reason, though they have clearly not promised you much wisdom.",
